A normal population has mean $\mu=50$ and standard deviation $\sigma=5$. For a sample of $n=100$, find:

a. $P(\bar X<47)$;

b. $P(47<\bar X<49.5)$;

c. the value $k$ such that $P(\bar X>k)=0.35$.

Ten percent of a large shipment of machine parts are defective. For random samples of 400 parts, find the proportion of samples with:

a. between 9% and 10% defective;

b. fewer than 8% defective.
